  {
   "text": "I've built the phone stand as a design in your creative project. It is 80 x 76 x 99 mm and passed its checks (watertight, 8 mm minimum wall). I haven't sliced or sent it to the printer.\n\nYou didn't say which phone, so I used the iPhone 15 (147.6 x 71.6 x 7.8 mm, per Apple's tech specs, no case). The phone leans back at 65 degrees on a 100 mm sloped support, with an 8 mm base and a 14 mm wide cable notch cut through the base in front of the phone's bottom edge. The 80 mm width, the 15 mm support thickness and the cable notch size are my guesses.\n\nTwo things to check before printing. The notch is a rough placement, so a real charging cable may need it moved or widened, and it's easy to adjust in Model. If you use a case, the slope may need more clearance. Tell me when you want it sliced and queued on your P1S with PLA."
  }
